      "llm_summary": "This database schema models a business environment involving customers, suppliers, parts, and orders. The `customer` table stores information about clients, linking them to their respective nations through the `nation` table, which in turn is connected to regions via the `region` table. Orders placed by customers are recorded in the `orders` table, with each order linked back to a specific customer and detailed line items stored in the `lineitem` table. Additionally, suppliers provide parts that can be included in orders; this relationship is captured through the `supplier`, `part`, and `partsupp` tables, which connect suppliers to the parts they supply and manage their availability and costs."
    },
    "sql_result": {
      "status": "success",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "sql": "SELECT \n    c.c_nationkey AS nation_key,\n    SUM(o.o_totalprice) AS total_order_value,\n    COUNT(o.o_orderkey) AS order_count\nFROM \n    tpch.customer c\nJOIN \n    tpch.orders o ON c.c_custkey = o.o_custkey\nGROUP BY \n    c.c_nationkey\nORDER BY \n    nation_key;",
